artner or our center of innovation in  west africa to document breeding  pipelines and identify simulation  scenarios and implement simulation code  we're focusing primarily on this coi on  the breeding strategy piece because they  are fairly advanced in terms of  deployment of breeding software  so they've already deployed bms to  manage their core breeding processes and  they're in the process of deploying  gigwa to manage their genomic  information  for our cois in west africa  they're really at the start of the  journey in terms of being able to  digitize their data and so we've been  working very closely with bms as a  partner  we've deployed the bms system and we've  completed training on the bms system  as mentioned we're currently mapping  broppy endpoints between genomic  management systems both gobi and digwa  and we have  initiated software development to begin  to start supporting genomic breeding use  cases  many of these programs aren't routinely  using genomic information yet but it is  on the horizon and we want to make sure  that these capabilities are in place  when they start doing routine genotyping  and finally significant progress has  been made in the development of  germplasm evaluation tools and this is  being done in collaboration with the  excellence in breeding we hope to see  the first release of this piece of  software  towards the end of the summer early fall  and we'll be continuing to enhance those  capabilities moving  forward with that i would just like to  thank everyone again for being here  and thanks again for the opportunity to  speak i look forward to the interactive  q a session  to be able to address any questions you  may have
 

